# The `?` twin of L5_14_hole_day_decision_read_is_hole (tally 2.3, #247; P10, H1): a decision on
# `dd = ?"which day?"` is never waited for; a read of its leg is that `?`. Before: RUN-ORDER.
=== m.tally
model b1hq
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind sweeps: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
kind tops: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sv2: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input pay: money PLN
input dd: date
input dt: date
move sweep: sweeps
  on dd
  reads sav
  leg cash from sav to world amount min(bal(sav), pay)
move top: tops
  on dt
  reads sv2, sweep
  leg cash from world to sv2 amount sum(t.cash.amount for t in sweeps over month_of(dt)) + 0 * bal(sv2)
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 100.00 PLN "c"
  dt = 2026-05-31 "c"
  dd = ?"which day?" "c"
  opening[sav] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
  opening[sv2] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
ask f: flows(top, 2026-05)
ask b: bal(sv2, 2026-06-30)
ask b_p5: bal(sv2, 2026-06-30) with dd = 2026-05-05
=== expect
b: ?"which day?" (dd)
  cut 2026-04-20
b_p5: 100.00 PLN
  pinned: dd = 2026-05-05
  cut 2026-04-20
f: ?"which day?" (dd)
  cut 2026-04-20
